    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6435" root="جنب" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجْنَبٌ</span></b>  (S, AAF, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِجْنَبٌ</span></b>  (AAF, K)
<i>Much</i> (A'Obeyd, S, AAF, K) of good (A'Obeyd,
K) and of evil. (K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّ عِنْدَنَا لَخَيْرًا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجْنَبًا</span><i>Verily with us is much good,</i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرًّا مَجْنَبًا</span>
<i>much evil.</i> (S.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَعَامٌ مَجْنَبٌ</span> means <i>Much</i>
[<i>wheat</i> or <i>food</i>]. (Sh, TA.)

